---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const skill = `---
name: prd-to-design-brief
description: Translate a PRD into an actionable design brief — user stories in user voice, required UI states, components needed, copy gaps, accessibility considerations, measurable outcomes, and open questions for PM.
---

You are a senior product designer reviewing a PRD that's about to become a design ticket. Your job is to translate prose-heavy PM-speak into an actionable design brief.

When given a PRD, return a structured markdown document with these sections (omit any section that genuinely doesn't apply, but be conservative — most do):

## 1. The job, in one line
A single sentence in user voice. Format: "As a [user type], I want to [action] so that [outcome]."

## 2. User stories
3–7 specific user stories, in user voice. Cover the happy path plus at least one edge case or error scenario.

## 3. Required UI states
For every screen or component the PRD implies, list the states that need to be designed. For each state, mark whether the PRD addresses it (✓), skips it (✗), or is ambiguous (?):
- Default / loaded
- Loading / pending
- Empty (first-time, before any user action)
- Empty (after action, e.g. "you've cleared everything")
- Error (network, validation, permission)
- Success
- Disabled / locked
- Focus / hover / active
- Long content / truncation

## 4. Components
Components you'll touch or create. For each: existing in the design system, or net-new? If net-new, why does this need to be its own component vs. a variant of something existing?

## 5. Copy required
List every piece of UI copy this feature needs (button labels, placeholders, error messages, success states, empty states, tooltips, microcopy). For each:
- The copy slot
- A first-pass suggestion in 4–8 words
- Whether final copy needs review by content design or legal

## 6. Accessibility
Checklist specific to this feature, not generic boilerplate:
- Keyboard navigation paths and order
- Screen reader announcements (live regions, status messages)
- Focus management (especially on modals, sheets, and async actions)
- Color contrast risks (call out specific token pairs if relevant)
- Motion and animation concerns
- ARIA roles and labels needed

## 7. Measurable outcomes
What will tell you this design worked? List 1–3 concrete metrics. For each: baseline (if stated), target (if stated), and a flag if either is missing from the PRD.

## 8. Open questions for PM
The most important things the PRD didn't answer. Numbered list, 5–10 questions, each phrased as a direct question. Sort by which one most blocks design from starting. Be specific — "What happens when the user has 1000 of these?" beats "What about scale?"

## 9. Risk flags
Things worth raising before you start:
- Scope creep risks
- Technical assumptions that may not hold
- Missing or stale user research
- Overlooked accessibility issues
- Compliance, legal, or privacy concerns
- Cross-platform parity gaps

## Tone
Write like a thoughtful senior designer who's seen this before. Direct but not snarky. Specific over generic. Reference UI patterns by name (e.g. "skeleton loader", "optimistic update", "non-blocking toast") when relevant.

## Length
Keep the whole brief under 800 words. Tight headlines, dense bullets, no preamble. Cut anything the reader can infer.
`;

const sampleInput = `# Notification Center MVP
Author: Janelle K. · Q2

## Background
Users have been asking for a centralized place to see their alerts. We currently surface alerts in three places (top bar, settings, dashboard), which creates a fragmented experience. Research shows 67% of power users miss critical alerts.

## Goal
Build a unified notification center accessible from every page.

## Requirements
- Clicking the bell icon in the top bar opens a panel
- Panel shows a list of recent notifications, most recent first
- Notifications can be dismissed individually or all at once
- Should be performant
- Accessible

## Success metrics
TBD

## Out of scope
- Notification preferences and settings
- Push notifications
- Email digests`;

const sampleOutput = `## 1. The job, in one line
As a power user, I want to see all my alerts in one place so I stop missing the critical ones.

## 2. User stories
- I open the notification center and see what needs my attention, ordered by recency.
- I dismiss a notification I've handled — it disappears from the list and won't come back.
- I clear all notifications at once when I'm caught up.
- I open the panel mid-task and close it without losing context.
- I receive a new notification while the panel is open — it should appear without flicker.
- (Edge) I have hundreds of notifications. The list stays performant and lets me reach the older ones.

## 3. Required UI states
**Bell icon (trigger):**
- Default ✓
- Active / panel open ?
- Unread badge (with count) ✗
- No unread (badge hidden) ✗

**Notification panel:**
- Default with notifications ✓
- Loading (initial fetch) ✗
- Empty (no notifications ever) ✗
- Empty (all cleared) ✗
- Error (fetch failed) ✗
- Long list (scroll, sticky header) ✗

**Single notification row:**
- Default ✓
- Unread vs. read ✗
- Hover / focus ✗
- Dismissing (animation) ✗

## 4. Components
- **Bell icon button** — likely exists; needs unread-count variant.
- **Notification panel** — net-new. A side sheet or popover from the bell. Probably a popover for desktop, full-screen sheet for mobile. Reason for net-new: it's a unique anchored container with its own scroll.
- **Notification row** — net-new. Reusable across panel and any future inbox view.
- **Empty state** — generic, but needs two flavors (never had any, just cleared).
- **Toast** for "All cleared" confirmation if undo is supported.

## 5. Copy required
- Bell aria-label: "Notifications, 3 unread" (4–6 words, dynamic count)
- Panel header: "Notifications"
- Empty (never): "All quiet here."
- Empty (cleared): "You're caught up."
- Dismiss action: "Dismiss" (button) — needs content design review for tone
- Clear-all action: "Clear all"
- Confirm clear-all: "Clear all 12 notifications?" — legal/content review
- Error: "Couldn't load notifications. Retry?"
- Time stamps: relative ("2 min ago") with a hover tooltip showing absolute timestamp

## 6. Accessibility
- Panel must be reachable via keyboard from the bell button (Enter / Space opens, Esc closes)
- Focus moves into the panel on open; returns to bell on close
- Each notification row is a focusable element with a clear label and a "dismiss" button as a child action
- Live region announcement on new notification arrival ("New notification") — but only when panel is closed, to avoid double-announcement
- Color contrast: unread indicator must not rely on color alone — pair with a dot or weight change
- Reduced-motion: replace dismiss-slide animation with a quick fade
- ARIA: role="dialog" or role="region" with aria-label="Notifications" on the panel; aria-live="polite" on the list

## 7. Measurable outcomes
- **Critical-alert miss rate** — baseline 67% (stated), target unstated. Flag: PM has not committed to a target.
- **Panel open events per active user / week** — baseline ✗, target ✗. Flag: no metric defined.
- **Time-to-dismiss after new notification** — would tell us if visibility actually improved. Flag: not in PRD.

## 8. Open questions for PM
1. Is unread state tracked per user, or does opening the panel mark all as read?
2. What's the maximum age of notifications shown? (Last 7 days? 30? Forever?)
3. Are notifications grouped by type or shown as a flat list?
4. What action does clicking a notification trigger — navigate, mark read, both?
5. Do "critical" notifications need different visual treatment, or is the alert center alone considered the fix?
6. Is "clear all" reversible (undo toast) or permanent?
7. What happens to a notification when the underlying object is deleted (e.g. a project mention when the project is gone)?
8. Mobile: full-screen sheet, drawer, or same popover at smaller width?
9. Are there permission scopes — i.e. can two users on the same workspace see different notifications?
10. Is there a "snooze" affordance, or is dismiss the only verb?

## 9. Risk flags
- The PRD calls "performant" without defining a threshold. Pin down: how many rows before virtualization is required?
- "Should be accessible" is not an a11y plan. Push for an explicit checklist.
- Three current surfaces (top bar, settings, dashboard) — what happens to those? Are we deprecating them, leaving them, or quietly orphaning?
- Out of scope says no preferences — but users will immediately ask "how do I turn off X?" Define the answer for the moment users ask, even if the feature ships later.
- 67% baseline is from "research" — was this a survey, support tickets, analytics? The intervention you design depends on whether the issue is visibility, frequency, or signal-to-noise.`;
---
<Layout
  pageClass="playground"
  title="PRD → Design brief — Ayo Omole"
  description="A Claude skill that turns a prose-heavy PRD into a structured, actionable design brief."
  palette={{ bg: '#f5ede1', fg: '#1f1409', accent: '#b8480f' }}
>
  <main class="sk">
    <header class="sk-head">
      <p class="sk-eyebrow">Play · 02 · Claude skill</p>
      <h1 class="sk-title">PRD → Design brief.</h1>
      <p class="sk-lede">
        Drop a PRD, get back the design brief you wish your PM had written. User stories in user voice, required UI states (with a check on which the PRD already covered), components, copy slots, a11y considerations, measurable outcomes, and the open questions worth chasing down before you start.
      </p>

      <div class="sk-meta">
        <div class="sk-meta-item">
          <span class="sk-meta-label">Type</span>
          <span class="sk-meta-value">Claude skill</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sk-meta-item">
          <span class="sk-meta-label">Use it in</span>
          <span class="sk-meta-value">Claude.ai · API</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sk-meta-item">
          <span class="sk-meta-label">Built for</span>
          <span class="sk-meta-value">Designers</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="sk-howto" aria-label="How to use">
      <h2 class="sk-section-title">How to use it</h2>
      <ol class="sk-steps">
        <li><strong>Copy the skill.</strong> The whole thing is below. One click.</li>
        <li><strong>Paste it into Claude.</strong> Either upload as a custom skill in Claude.ai, or include it as the system prompt via the API.</li>
        <li><strong>Drop your PRD.</strong> Paste the document text into the chat. Claude returns a structured design brief in markdown.</li>
        <li><strong>Use it.</strong> Copy the brief into a Figma frame, a Linear ticket, or a Notion doc. Argue about the open questions before you draw a single rectangle.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="sk-example" aria-label="Example">
      <h2 class="sk-section-title">Example</h2>
      <div class="sk-example-grid">
        <div class="sk-example-col">
          <div class="sk-example-head">
            <span class="sk-example-label">Input</span>
            <span class="sk-example-sub">A typical thin PRD</span>
          </div>
          <pre class="sk-code"><code>{sampleInput}</code></pre>
        </div>
        <div class="sk-example-col">
          <div class="sk-example-head">
            <span class="sk-example-label">Output</span>
            <span class="sk-example-sub">The brief Claude returns</span>
          </div>
          <pre class="sk-code sk-code--out"><code>{sampleOutput}</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="sk-skill" aria-label="The skill">
      <header class="sk-skill-head">
        <h2 class="sk-section-title">The skill</h2>
        <button type="button" class="sk-action sk-action--primary" data-action="copy">
          <span class="sk-action-text">Copy skill</span>
        </button>
      </header>
      <pre class="sk-code sk-code--skill" id="sk-content"><code>{skill}</code></pre>
    </section>
  </main>

  <style>
    .sk {
      max-width: var(--site-max-width);
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem) var(--site-edge) clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem);
      box-sizing: border-box;
      color: var(--foreground-color);
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    }

    .sk-head {
      max-width: 60ch;
    }
    .sk-eyebrow {
      font-family: var(--sansFont);
      font-size: var(--text-small);
      color: rgba(var(--foreground-color-rgb), 0.5);
      margin: 0 0 1rem;
    }
    .sk-title {
      font-family: var(--titleFont);
      font-size: var(--text-display);
      line-height: 0.98;
      letter-spacing: -0.035em;
      font-weight: 400;
      margin: 0 0 clamp(1rem, 2vw, 1.5rem);
    }
    .sk-lede {
      font-family: var(--sansFont);
      font-size: var(--text-large);
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: rgba(var(--foreground-color-rgb), 0.7);
      margin: 0 0 clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    }

    .sk-meta {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
      padding-top: 1.25rem;
      border-top: 1px solid rgba(var(--foreground-color-rgb), 0.12);
    }
    .sk-meta-item {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.25rem;
    }
    .sk-meta-label {
      font-family: var(--sansFont);
      font-size: var(--text-mini);
      color: rgba(var(--foreground-color-rgb), 0.5);
      letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    }
    .sk-meta-value {
      font-family: var(--sansFont);
      font-size: var(--text-small);
      font-weight: 500;
      color: var(--foreground-color);
    }

    .sk-section-title {
      font-family: var(--titleFont);
      font-size: var(--text-h3);
      line-height: 1.1;
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
      font-weight: 400;
      margin: 0 0 clamp(1rem, 2vw, 1.5rem);
    }

    .sk-steps {
      counter-reset: step;
      list-style: none;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: clamp(0.875rem, 1.5vw, 1.25rem);
      max-width: 60ch;
    }
    .sk-steps li {
      counter-increment: step;
      position: relative;
      padding-left: 2.5rem;
      font-family: var(--sansFont);
      font-size: var(--text-medium);
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: rgba(var(--foreground-color-rgb), 0.78);
    }
    .sk-steps li::before {
      content: counter(step);
      position: absolute;
      left: 0;
      top: 0;
      width: 1.75rem;
      height: 1.75rem;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: var(--fg);
      color: var(--accent-bright, var(--bg));
      display: grid;
      place-items: center;
      font-family: var(--monoFont);
      font-size: var(--text-mini);
      font-weight: 500;
    }
    .sk-steps strong { color: var(--foreground-color); font-weight: 600; }

    .sk-example-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 1.5rem);
    }
    @media (max-width: 880px) {
      .sk-example-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
    }
    .sk-example-col {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.75rem;
    }
    .sk-example-head { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.125rem; }
    .sk-example-label {
      font-family: var(--sansFont);
      font-size: var(--text-small);
      font-weight: 500;
      color: var(--foreground-color);
    }
    .sk-example-sub {
      font-family: var(--sansFont);
      font-size: var(--text-mini);
      color: rgba(var(--foreground-color-rgb), 0.55);
    }

    .sk-code {
      margin: 0;
      padding: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 1.5rem);
      background: #ffffff;
      border-radius: clamp(0.75rem, 1.5vw, 1.25rem);
      font-family: var(--monoFont);
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
      color: var(--foreground-color);
      overflow-x: auto;
      max-height: 30rem;
      overflow-y: auto;
      box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.04);
      white-space: pre-wrap;
      word-break: break-word;
    }
    .sk-code code { font-family: inherit; }
    .sk-code--out {
      background: rgba(var(--foreground-color-rgb), 0.04);
      box-shadow: none;
    }
    .sk-code--skill {
      max-height: none;
      background: var(--fg);
      color: var(--accent-bright, var(--bg));
    }

    .sk-skill-head {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 1rem;
      margin-bottom: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 1.5rem);
    }
    .sk-skill-head .sk-section-title { margin: 0; }

    .sk-action {
      padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--fg);
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: var(--fg);
      color: var(--accent-bright, var(--bg));
      font-family: var(--sansFont);
      font-size: var(--text-small);
      font-weight: 500;
      cursor: pointer;
      transition: transform 240ms cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
    }
    .sk-action:hover { transform: translateY(-1px); }
    .sk-action.is-confirmed {
      background: var(--accent);
      color: var(--bg);
      border-color: var(--accent);
    }
  </style>

  <script is:inline data-astro-rerun>
    (() => {
      const btn = document.querySelector('[data-action="copy"]');
      const code = document.getElementById('sk-content');
      if (!btn || !code) return;
      btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        navigator.clipboard.writeText(code.textContent).then(() => {
          const txt = btn.querySelector('.sk-action-text');
          const original = txt.textContent;
          btn.classList.add('is-confirmed');
          txt.textContent = 'Copied!';
          setTimeout(() => {
            btn.classList.remove('is-confirmed');
            txt.textContent = original;
          }, 1400);
        });
      });
    })();
  </script>
</Layout>
